==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_LeastPrivilege_MatrixGate  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_LeastPrivilege_MatrixGate.als
    rationale: Removing the matrix-gate fact lets Alloy construct a permitted operation whose (role,endpoint) cell is denied by the permission matrix — e.g., a compliance officer reading a clinical record. LeastPrivilege should catch this.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_007_ComplianceNoClinicalRead
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_007_ComplianceNoClinicalRead: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_LeastPrivilege_ClinicianCT  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_LeastPrivilege_ClinicianCT.als
    rationale: Removing the clinician-care-team gate lets Alloy invent a permitted clinician access for a record on which the clinician has no active care-team membership — exactly the FR-004 violation the OwnershipBasedAccess assertion is meant to catch.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_004_ClinicianCareTeamGate
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_004_ClinicianCareTeamGate: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditOnePerAuthenticatedOp  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_AuditOnePerAuthenticatedOp.als
    rationale: Removing the one-audit-per-authenticated-op fact lets the model invent an authenticated record-access operation with no matching audit entry, which violates FR-013/SC-001/SC-002.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_013_AuditCompleteness
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NotesViaPermittedAppendOp  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_NotesViaPermittedAppendOp.als
    rationale: Removing the note-justification fact lets a clinical note exist without a corresponding permitted append operation — modelling either a mutation that bypassed the API or a synthetic note appearing out of thin air, both forbidden by FR-012's append-only contract.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_012_NotesAppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_NotesAppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ByteEquivalentForbidden  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_ByteEquivalentForbidden.als
    rationale: Removing the canonical-forbidden fact lets Alloy construct a denied operation whose response is observationally distinguishable from the byte-equivalent 403 envelope — exactly the existence-leak scenario FR-008/SC-003 forbids.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_008_ByteEquivalent403
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_008_ByteEquivalent403: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuthRequiredOrDenied  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_AuthRequiredOrDenied.als
    rationale: Removing the authentication-boundary fact lets the model invent an unauthenticated operation that nonetheless reaches a Permitted outcome, violating FR-001's 'unauthenticated rejected before any record dereference' guarantee.
    expected to FAIL: AuthRequiredEverywhere, FR_001_AuthRequired
      - AuthRequiredEverywhere: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_001_AuthRequired: FAIL (expected)

